# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sabr / Sirat Khushu push+auth server — environment template.
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is git-ignored) and fill in real values.
# Only the SMTP block is REQUIRED for password-reset emails; everything else is optional.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Email password reset (REQUIRED for "forgot password" to actually send a code) ──
# To send from a real Gmail account, create an APP PASSWORD (NOT your normal password):
#   Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification (turn on) → App passwords → generate.
# Paste the 16-character app password (spaces removed) into SMTP_PASS.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-16-char-gmail-app-password
MAIL_FROM="Sirat Khushu" <you@gmail.com>
# SMTP_SECURE=true          # set only if you use port 465

# ── Admin portal at /admin (REQUIRED to enable it) ──
# The dashboard over every account, push subscription and storage figure on this server.
# With this UNSET, /admin serves setup instructions and nothing else — it fails closed on
# purpose, because an admin page that is open by default would expose every account.
# Use a long random string (this is YOUR key — never a user's password):
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# ADMIN_KEY=paste-a-long-random-string-here

# ── Optional: lock writes to your app only ──
# Set the SAME long random string in the app (Settings → Background reminders → App key).
# APP_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# ── Optional: web-push reminder keys (auto-generated on first boot if omitted) ──
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@yourdomain.com

# ── Deployment hardening ──
# On a BARE server with no fronting proxy, set TRUST_PROXY=0 so clients can't spoof
# X-Forwarded-For past the rate limiters. Behind Render/Railway/a proxy, leave it unset.
# TRUST_PROXY=0
